.TH AVR\-VM\-PORT\-FORWARD 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-port-forward \- Forward a local port to a TCP port on the VM over SSH.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm port-forward
[OPTIONS] VM_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Forward a local port to a TCP port on the VM over SSH.
.PP
The generic primitive behind `avr vm rdp` / `avr vm vnc`: opens 127.0.0.1:<local-port> -> <VM>:<port> through the VM's SSH endpoint, where <port> is set by --port, and holds it open until Ctrl-C. Bring your own client.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Guest-side TCP port to forward (e.g. 8080). (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-local\-port\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Local port to bind (default: an unused port).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIPATH\fR
Private key file to pass to ssh as -i.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the ssh command and exit, without opening the tunnel.
